# Control twin of tests/models/feature_coverage/ss_local_fcn_const_global.bngl
# for the issue #40 cost guard (local_fcn_rescan_gate_test).
#
# Identical in every respect but one: the bare observable `Vol` in the local
# function is replaced by the parameter `VolConst`, which holds the value
# `Vol` has at every event of that model's run.  Same arithmetic, same rate,
# same RNG stream, same trajectory — but the rule no longer reads an
# observable, so it never enters `global_dep_local_rules` and takes the
# ordinary affected-molecule delta path throughout.
#
# That makes it the cost floor: whatever this twin costs is what the model
# reading the constant `Vol` must also cost, because no rescan it could have
# performed can change a single per-instance rate.  Before #40 it cost ~200x
# more.
#
# Kept out of tests/models/feature_coverage/ deliberately — it adds no
# feature coverage over its twin, only a timing baseline, so it does not
# belong in a suite that runs 20 NFsim replicates per model on every push.

begin model
begin parameters
    X0        20000    # reactive:  Aphos(x) = 1, flips at kf*VolConst
    I0         2000    # inert:     Aphos(x) = 0, must never fire
    kf        2.0e-4
    VolConst     50    # the value the twin's `Vol` observable holds throughout
end parameters

begin molecule types
    V()
    A(m~0~1,p~0~1)
end molecule types

begin seed species
    V()              50
    A(m~0,p~1)       X0
    A(m~0,p~0)       I0
end seed species

begin observables
    Molecules  Vol    V()
    Molecules  Aphos  A(p~1)
    Molecules  Aoff   A(m~0)
    Molecules  Aon    A(m~1)
end observables

begin functions
    # The twin writes `kf*Vol*Aphos(x)`.  Only the middle factor differs.
    aflip(x) = kf*VolConst*Aphos(x)
end functions

begin reaction rules
    RA: A(m~0)%x -> A(m~1)%x    aflip(x)
end reaction rules
end model

begin actions
simulate({method=>"nf",t_end=>100,n_steps=>20})
end actions
